<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετραῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of
				a rock</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					589
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>living on</i> or <i>among the rocks</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύλλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.231
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					304.3
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νύμφαι π</span>.
			<i>rock</i>-Nymphs, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				805
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					669
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π. τῶν ἰχθυδίων</span>
			<i>rock</i>-fish, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Com.
				62.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sotad.Com.
				1.22
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετραῖα</span>, as a class of
			marine animals, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελάγια,
			αἰγιαλώδη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				488b7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				598a11
			</span></i> ; <i>growing on</i> or <i>among rocks</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rocky</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκάλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1019
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάφος π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				151
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δειράς, λέπας, χθών,
				ἄντρα</span>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				697
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				120
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				382
			</span></i> (s.v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IA</u>
				1082
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					570b26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πετραῖος</span>, epith. of Poseidon in
			Thessaly, as he <i>who clave the rocks</i> of Tempe, and drained
			Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.138
			</span></i>.</div>
